.SH "NAME"
nvme-rpmb-read-config \- Read the RPMB device configuration block
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.nf
\fInvme\fR [<global\-options>] \fIrpmb read\-config\fR <device>
                        [\-\-msgfile=<data\-file> | \-f <data\-file>]
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
Reads the 512 byte device configuration block from RPMB target 0 of the NVMe device\&.
.sp
If \-\-msgfile is not given, a summary of the boot partition protection and lock state is printed to STDOUT instead of the raw configuration block\&.
.sp
The <device> parameter is mandatory and an NVMe character device (ex: /dev/nvme0) must be specified\&.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.PP
\-f <data\-file>, \-\-msgfile=<data\-file>
.RS 4
Name of the file the read configuration block is written to\&. If an existing file is given, data is appended to it\&. If not given, a summary is printed to STDOUT instead\&.
.RE
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.sp
The following options are defined at the top\-level nvme command and are available to this subcommand:
.PP
\-\-dry\-run
.RS 4
Print the command that would be executed, but do not actually execute it\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no\-ioctl\-probing
.RS 4
Disable probing for 64\-bit IOCTL support\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no\-retries
.RS 4
Disable retry logic on transient errors\&.
.RE
.PP
\-o <fmt>, \-\-output\-format=<fmt>
.RS 4
Set the reporting format to
\fInormal\fR,
\fItabular, \*(Aqjson\fR, or
\fIbinary\fR\&. Only one output format may be used at a time\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-output\-format\-version=<version>
.RS 4
Select the output format version\&. Version
\fI1\fR
uses the original field naming, while version
\fI2\fR
(default) provides more consistent and script\-friendly field names\&.
.RE
.PP
\-\-timeout=<ms>
.RS 4
Set the timeout for the command in milliseconds\&.
.RE
.PP
\-v, \-\-verbose
.RS 4
Increase the level of detail in the output\&. May be specified multiple times to further increase verbosity\&.
.RE
.sp
These options can also be set as machine\-wide defaults in nvme\-cli\&.conf(5)\&. A command\-line flag always overrides the file\&.
